  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-9 Start
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: My brother Paciano gave me 700 pesos for my journey. I appreciate his
      support. In turn, I will make good use of this money during my voyage. My sister
      Saturnina gave me a valuable diamond ring which might help me when there's
      an emergency. I will treasure this and make this my reminder, to keep holding
      on
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: A distant relative secured me a passport, as it is a necessity if I
      want to leave the country. In there, my name is Jose Mercado so that there
      will be no issues that will arise on my journey. I eventually left Calamba.
      I made my way to the steamer, changing horses twice in five hours. The next
      morning, I embarked on the steamer, made a pencil sketch of Manila, as it will
      be a long time before I return to my homeland
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: My journey started off with me going to Singapore. I was surprised
      at the fact that the natives of the land were confident in their rights and
      not fearful of the authorities. It made me admire them in a way, as we Filipinos
      are afraid of the Spaniards
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: When I arrived in Singapore, I transferred to a French mail Steamer
      and had an interesting time making myself understood when I was on board. I
      studied a bit of French, though it didn't help the Frenchmen understand what
      I wanted to say. I resorted to speaking in Latin, made signs, and in extreme
      cases, drew pictures. It interested the officers from the cartoon class and
      I was given the freedom to roam around the ship and my voyage went smoothly.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I disembarked at Marseilles, saw a bit of the famous port, then made
      my way to Barcelona. In comparison to when I arrived at Marseilles, they were
      very courteous of tourists. The Spanish disregarded tourists, which left a
      smidge of a sour taste in my mouth. I digress
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
